          %title Superalgebra
          %blockquote
            %p
              this entry is the first section of “
              %span.newWikiWord>
                supergeometry and superphysics
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/geommetry+of+physics+--+supergeometry+and+superphysics"} ?
              ”,
            %p
              which itself is one chapter of “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"}> geometry of physics
              ”
            %p
              next section:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %p
              previous chapter:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} categories and toposes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometry"} Klein geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            the fundamental geometric concept is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+group"} symmetry group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of the local model
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are reflected in their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+representations"} categories of representations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner+classification"} Wigner classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+objects"} irreducible objects
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            label the possible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particle"} fundamental particle
            species on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            as the actual fundamental concept, then the natural question is that of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka reconstruction
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(G)
            for some symmetry group
            = succeed "?" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigid+monoidal+category"} rigid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            subject only to a mild size constraint this is answered by
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"} Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            (theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheTheorem"}
            below): all of them are, but only if we allow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to be a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"}> supergroup
            ”.
          %h1#superalgebra Superalgebra
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#TensorProductsAndMonoidalCategories"} Tensor products and Super vector spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#CommutativeAlgebraInTensorCategories"} Commutative algebra in tensor categories and Affine super-spaces
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#monoids_in_monoidal_categories_and_supercommutative_superalgebra"} Monoids in monoidal categories and Supercommutative superalgebra
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#example_super_lie_algebras_and_super_algebras"}
                    Example: Super Lie algebras and Super
                    = succeed "-algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
