                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ZGradedSupercommutativeSuperAlgebra"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                    \-Graded Supercommutative superalgebra
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#affine_superschemes"} Affine superschemes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ModulesInTensorCategories"} Modules in tensor categories and Super vector bundles
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#propposition"} Propposition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#GroupsAsHopfAlgebras"} Super-Groups as super-commutative Hopf algebras
              %li
                %a{:href => "#LinearRepresentationsAsComodules"} Linear super-representations as Comodules
              %li
                %a{:href => "#FiberFunctors"} Super Fiber functors and their automorphism supergroups
              %li
                %a{:href => "#superexterior_powers_and_schur_functors"} Super-exterior powers and Schur functors
              %li
                %a{:href => "#_tannaka_duality_between_tensor_categories_and_supergroups"} Tannaka duality between tensor categories and supergroups
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %p
            The beauty of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            below) is that it is just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"}> internal
            ” to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} on categories and toposes
            for the basic concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            (i.e. a super
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+group"} symmetry-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} super-symmetry
            group) is just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebra"} commutative Hopf algebra
            internal to super vector spaces. The beauty of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            equipped with the
            %em unique
            non-trivial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric braiding
            %em all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            subject to a mild size constraint are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+representations"} categories of representations
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheTheorem"}
            below (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne%27s+theorem+on+tensor+categories"}> Deligne's theorem on tensor categories
            ).
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/DeligneSuperFiberFunctor.png", :width => "600"}/
          %p Here we introduce and explain all this.
          %p
            We start by introducing the basic concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            along with the basic examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#TensorProductsAndMonoidalCategories"} Tensor products and Super vector spaces
          %p
            This allows to speak of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to tensor categories. Specializing this to the tensor category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            yields
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            of these are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+variety"} affine
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+schemes"} super schemes
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#CommutativeAlgebraInTensorCategories"} Commutative algebra in tensor categories and Affine super-spaces
          %p
            In the same dual spirit,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+bundles"} super vector bundles
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+schemes"} affine super schemes
            are algebraically incarnated as (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated+object"} finitely generated
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projctive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ModulesInTensorCategories"} Modules in tensor categories and Super vector bundles
          %p
            Next we introduce the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebras"} commutative Hopf algebras
            and explain how these are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebras"} commutative Hopf algebras
            internal to the tensor category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+Hopf+algebras"} supercommutative Hopf algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GroupsAsHopfAlgebras"} Super-Groups as Super-commutative Hopf algebras
          %p
            Then we discuss how under this relationo, then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representations"} linear representations
            of groups correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodules"} comodules
            over their formally dual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebras"} commutative Hopf algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+representations"} categories of representations
            of groups and of super-representations of super-groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#LinearRepresentationsAsComodules"} Linear super-representations as comodules
          %p
            All such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+representations"} categories of representations
            carry a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            that sends any representation to its underlying representation space. Simple as this is, fiber functors turn out to be the key concept in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %em abstractly
            defined super fiber functor gives rise to an affine algebraic supergroup, namely its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#FiberFunctors"} Super Fiber functors and their automorphism supergroups
          %p
            And in fact, under mild conditions this supergorup of automorphisms of the fiber functor of a tensor category is such that the tensor category is equivalently its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            for
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"} Pierre Deligne
            gives
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            = succeed "." do
              %em raison d’être
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#TannakaDualityForTensorCategoriesAndSupergroups"} Tannaka duality between tensor categories and supergroups
          %h2#TensorProductsAndMonoidalCategories Tensor products and Super vector spaces
          #VectorSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_k
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Categories"}> this Def.
              ) whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
                  between these.
            %p
              When the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is understood or when its precise nature is irrelevant, we will often notationally suppress it and speak of just the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              of vector spaces.
            %p
              This is the category inside which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
              takes place.
          %p
            Of course the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            has some special properties. Not only are its objects “linear spaces”, but the whole category inherits linear structure of sorts. This is traditionally captured by the following terminology for
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+and+abelian+categories"} additive and abelian categories
          #AdditiveAndAbelianCategories.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Categories"}> this Def.
              ).
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Say that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  has
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
                  if it has
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+coproducts"} finite coproducts
                  and if the canonical comparison morphism between these is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \oplus W
                  for the direct sum of two objects of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  Say that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
                  if it has
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
                  and in addition it is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} enriched in abelian groups
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  is equipped with the structure of an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                  such that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  of morphisms is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
              %li
                %p
                  Say that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is an
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                  if it is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
                  and has property that its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                  are precisely the inclusions of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
                  and its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
                  are precisely the projections onto
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"} cokernels
          %p
            We also make the following definition of
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrichment
            to require on a linear category:
          #LinearCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              (or more generally just a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear category
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveAndAbelianCategories"}
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
                  have the structure of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
                  (generally
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  of morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
            %p
              and the underlying additive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              structure of these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
              is that of the underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %p
              In other words, a
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              with the additional structure of a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              (generally
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "-enriched)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enrichment
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveAndAbelianCategories"}
              is obtained from the
              = succeed "-enrichment" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Vect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect \to Ab
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              between
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functor"} linear functor
              if its component functions on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
              with respect to the given
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_k
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VectorSpaces"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear category
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearCategory"}
            %p
              Here the abstract
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              is the usual direct sum of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V,W
              two
              = succeed "-vector" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{Vect}(V,W)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon V \to W
              is given by “pointwise” multiplication and addition of functions:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c_1 \phi_1 + c_2 \phi_2)
                    \\;\colon\,
                    v \;\mapsto\;
                    c_1 \phi_1(v) + c_2 \phi_2(v)
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1, c_2 \in k
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_1, \phi_2 \in Hom_{Vect}(V,W)
          %p
            Recall the basic construction of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
          #TensorProductOfVectorSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              over some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1, V_2 \in Vect_k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
              is the vector space denoted
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \otimes_k V_2 \;\in\; Vect
            %p
              whose elements are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
              of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1,v_2)
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V_i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c v_1 , v_2) \;\sim\; (v_1, c v_2)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (v_1 + v'_1 , v_2) \; \sim \; (v_1,v_2) + (v'_1, v_2)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (v_1 , v_2 + v'_2) \; \sim \; (v_1,v_2) + (v_1, v'_2)
            %p
              More abstractly this means that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
              is the vector space characterized by the fact that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it receives a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        V_1 \times V_2 \longrightarrow V_1 \otimes V_2
                %p
                  (out of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  of the underlying sets)
              %li
                %p
                  any other
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        V_1 \times V_2 \longrightarrow V_3
                %p
                  factors through the above bilinear map via a unique
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mn 2
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi bilinear
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mn 3
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↗
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo ∃
                                      %mo !
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi linear
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mn 1
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        V_1 \times V_2 &amp;\overset{bilinear}{\longrightarrow}&amp; V_3
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\exists ! \, linear}}
                        \\\
                        V_1 \otimes_k V_2
                        }
          %p
            The existence of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductOfVectorSpaces"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            of vector spaces with extra structure, which is a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"}> categorification
            ” of the familiar structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            and therefore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            operation are also called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#MonoidalCategory"}> this Def.
            ):
          #MonoidalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"}> monoidal category
                )
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              equipped with
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ×
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\otimes
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathcal{C}
                %p
                  out of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  with itself, called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %li
                %p an object
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        1 \in \mathcal{C}
                %p
                  called the
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
                  or
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        a
                        \\;\colon\;
                        ((-)\otimes (-)) \otimes (-)
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        (-) \otimes ((-)\otimes(-))
                %p
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              %li#MonoidalCategoryUnitors
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\ell
                        \\;\colon\;
                        (1 \otimes (-))
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        (-)
                %p
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+unitor"} left unitor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        r \;\colon\; (-) \otimes 1 \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} (-)
                %p
                  called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+unitor"} right unitor
            %p
              such that the following two kinds of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagrams commute
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> triangle identity
                  \:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi a
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi x
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mn 1
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi y
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ρ
                                      %mi x
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %msub
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mi y
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mi x
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %msub
                                      %mi λ
                                      %mi y
                              %mtd
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp; (x \otimes 1) \otimes y &amp;\stackrel{a_{x,1,y}}{\longrightarrow} &amp; x \otimes (1 \otimes y)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\rho_x \otimes 1_y}\searrow
                        \&amp;&amp; \swarrow_{1_x \otimes \lambda_y}
                        \&amp;
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        x \otimes y
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        }
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagon+identity"} pentagon identity
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi w
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi α
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi w
                                          %mo ⊗
                                          %mi x
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi y
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi z
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi α
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi w
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi x
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi y
                                          %mo ⊗
                                          %mi z
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi w
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi z
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi w
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %msub
                                          %mi α
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi w
                                            %mo ,
                                            %mi x
                                            %mo ,
                                            %mi y
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %msub
                                      %mi id
                                      %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi id
                                        %mi w
                                      %mo ⊗
                                      %msub
                                        %mi α
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi x
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi y
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi z
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi w
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi z
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi α
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi w
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi x
                                        %mo ⊗
                                        %mi y
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi z
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi w
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; (w \otimes x) \otimes (y \otimes z)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\alpha_{w \otimes x, y, z}}}\nearrow
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\searrow^{\mathrlap{\alpha_{w,x,y \otimes z}}}
                        \\\
                        ((w \otimes x ) \otimes y) \otimes z
                        \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                        (w \otimes (x \otimes (y \otimes z)))
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{\alpha_{w,x,y}} \otimes id_z }\downarrow
                        \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                        \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{ id_w \otimes \alpha_{x,y,z} }}
                        \\\
                        (w \otimes (x \otimes y)) \otimes z
                        \&amp;&amp; \underset{\alpha_{w,x \otimes y, z}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                        w \otimes ( (x \otimes y) \otimes z )
                        }
          %p As expected, we have the following basic example:
          #VectAsAMonoidalCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_k
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the abstract
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_k
                  from def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductOfVectorSpaces"}
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  itself, regarded as a 1-dimensional vector space over itself;
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
                  is the map that on representing
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
                  acts as
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mn 3
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\alpha_{V_{1}, V_2, V_3}
                        \\;\colon\;
                        ((v_1, v_2), v_3) \mapsto (v_1, (v_2,v_3))
              %li
                %p
                  the left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
                  is the map that on representing
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
                  is given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\ell_{V} \colon (k,v) \mapsto k v
                %p and the right unitor is similarly given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mi V
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi k
                        %mi v
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        r_V \colon (v,k) \mapsto k v
                        \\,.
            %p
              That this satisifes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagon+identity"} pentagon identity
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
          %p
            But the point of the abstract definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            is that there are also more exotic examples. The followig one is just a minimal enrichment of example
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VectAsAMonoidalCategory"}
          #GradedVectorSpacesAsAMonoidaCategory.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              (or in fact just a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of vector spaces labeled by the elements in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V = \underset{g \in G}{\oplus} V_g
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \;\colon\; V \longrightarrow W
            %p
              of
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
              that respects this direct sum structure, hence equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi g
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi_g \;\colon\; V_g \longrightarrow W_g
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi = \underset{g \in G}{\oplus} \phi_g
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Vect
                        %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect^G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              which on the underlying vector spaces is just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
              from def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductOfVectorSpaces"}
              = succeed "-grading" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi G
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                            %mo =
                            %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (V \otimes W)_g
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{{g_1, g_2 \in G} \atop {g_1 g_2 = g}}{\oplus}
                    V_{g_1} \otimes_k V_{g_2}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              for the tensor product is the ground field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi k
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi g
                              %mo =
                              %mi e
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1_g
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    k &amp; | g = e
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; | otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
              are just those of the monoidal structure on plain vector spaces, from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VectAsAMonoidalCategory"}
          %p
            One advantage of abstracting the concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            is that it allows to prove general statements uniformly for all kinds of tensor products, familar ones and more exotic ones. The following lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kel1"}
            and remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoherenceForMonoidalCategories"}
            are two important such statements.
          #kel1.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Kelly64"}> Kelly 64
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitors"} unitors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              satisfy the following conditions:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_1 = r_1 \;\colon\; 1 \otimes 1 \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} 1
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  for all objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in \mathcal{C}
                  the following
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagrams commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi α
                                        %mrow
                                          %mn 1
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi x
                                          %mo ,
                                          %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ℓ
                                        %mi x
                                      %mo ⊗
                                      %msub
                                        %mi id
                                        %mi y
                              %mtd
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi ℓ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi x
                                        %mo ⊗
                                        %mi y
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        (1 \otimes x) \otimes y  &amp; &amp;
                        \\\
                        {}^\mathllap{\alpha_{1, x, y}} \downarrow
                        \&amp; \searrow^\mathrlap{\ell_x \otimes id_y} &amp;
                        \\\
                        1 \otimes (x \otimes y)
                        \&amp; \underset{\ell_{x \otimes y}}{\longrightarrow} &amp; x \otimes y
                        }
                        \\,;
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
