          %h2#FiberFunctors Super Fiber functors and their automorphism supergroups
          %p
            The first step in exhibiting a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            as being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            is to exhibit its objects as having an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} underlying
            representation space of sorts, and then an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            represented on that space. Hence a necessary condition on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is that there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \;\colon\; \mathcal{A} \longrightarrow \mathcal{V}
          %p
            to some other
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            satisfies a list of properties, in particular it should be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+functor"} symmetric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          %p
            Such functors are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functors"} fiber functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathcal{V}
            we find the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega^{-1}(V)
            of that “bundle”, consisting of all those objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            whose underlying object in the given
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            The main point of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            of tensor categories is the observation that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            on that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            (i.e. via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            of functors). In good cases then this may be turned around, and the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of a fiber functor is identified with the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            for which the objects in its fibers are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+reconstruction"} Tannaka reconstruction
          %p There are slight variants on what one requires of a fiber functor. For the present purpose we fix the following definition
          #FiberFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_41 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              be two
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorCategory"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  all
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+of+finite+length"} objects have finite length
              %li
                %p
                  all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+spaces"} hom spaces
                  are of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
