                  Aut(\omega) \in Grp
          %p for this automorphism group.
          %p
            So far this is a group without geometric structure (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            (super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"}> algebraic geometry
            ) exhibited by a rule for what the “geometrically parameterized families” of its elements are. (For exposition of this perspective see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
          %p
            Concretely, this means that for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+scheme"} affine super scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            (def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underline{Aut}(\omega)(Spec(A))
                  \\in
                  Set
          %p
            of
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(\omega)
            is. In fact, under parameter-wise multiplication in the group, any such set must inherit group structure, so that we should have not one discrete group, but a system of them, labeled by supercommutative superalgebras:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underline{Aut}(\omega)(Spec(A))
                  \\in
                  Grp
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
